@prefix cv:   <https://chatmangpt.com/ontology/challenger-value#> .
@prefix odrl: <http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/> .

# This pack's own ontology.ttl uses cv:ChallengerProjectionPolicy as an
# individual value of paas:innovationPolicy (a cross-pack reference into
# challenger-value-framing-pack). challenger-value-framing-pack's own
# ontology.ttl asserts real facts about that individual (cv:authorityCeiling,
# odrl:prohibition) but -- like this fixture -- never types it as a
# rdfs:Class/owl:Class, so the marketplace's cross-pack-reference checker
# (scripts/check_cross_pack_references.py) cannot exempt it via the
# vocabulary-use path (that path is reserved for genuine class/property
# reuse, not instance-value references). Per that script's own documented
# design (its module docstring), the correct admission path for exactly
# this shape -- an external pack's real individual, used as a real
# property value, not a class -- is this pack's own opt-in
# qualification/consumer.ttl restating the one type this pack's own usage
# actually relies on: cv:ChallengerProjectionPolicy is a real ODRL policy
# individual (it carries odrl:prohibition facts in its home pack), so:
cv:ChallengerProjectionPolicy a odrl:Policy .
